WEBVTT

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.230
<b>This program is a work of fiction. The characters, organizations, locations, cases, etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.</b>

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.460
Now, then...

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.710
Out of bullets, are we?

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.680
Well... I am, at least.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.860
How about we call a truce?

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.930
I haven't seen you around before.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.680
Are you what people call a bounty hunter?

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:24.240
I was pretty certain I knew what most 
of the assassins around here looked like.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.140
Are you a newbie?

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.270
You really shouldn't get into 
such a dangerous line of work.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.780
Your parents are probably 
very worried about you.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.660
All right, question time.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:41.400
Let's see... What's your name?

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:43.660
What?

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.310
Your name.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.040
Simple, no?

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.940
I'm sorry, maybe I wasn't clear enough.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.620
You see, I'm flirting with you right now.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.100
I have a bounty on my head, after all,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.050
so I don't get that many 
chances to talk to girls.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:06.600
This is clearly some kind of 
fate, so... How about it?

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.980
Tell me your name.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:05.930
Hello?

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.680
<i>Look, Chateau. I told you 
not to act on your own.</i>

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.970
<i>Come back here this instant.</i>

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.070
I'm terribly sorry, sir,
but my battery is about to run out.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.260
I'm hanging up now.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:19.820
<i>Uh—</i>

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.170
Hey!

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.370
Wait a second, Chateau!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.580
Aw, were you rejected again?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.210
m 0 0 l 0 -15 l 75 -15 l 75 0

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.210
<b>Ritzland Support Company Representative
Euripides Ritzland</b>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.210
That newbie is such a handful.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.580
It's because you spoil her, sir.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.580
m 0 0 l 0 -15 l 75 -15 l 75 0

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.580
<b>Ritzland Support Company Accounting & Admin
Nickname: Jim  Real Name: ???</b>

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.700
Well, what am I supposed to do?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:43.520
I guess you wouldn't know how 
to deal with young women.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.840
You really know how to burn someone.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.260
She's the daughter of my father's benefactor.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.260
m 0 0 l 0 -15 l 75 -15 l 75 0

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.260
<b>Ritzland Support Company Staff
Chateau Dankworth</b>

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.600
So how did she become a bounty hunter?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.460
Huh?

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.490
Actually, I never asked.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.110
But you know...

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.880
Chateau's done quite a bit this month.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.990
She managed to secure 
two targets on her own.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:17.000
Maybe Chateau has someone 
really dangerous backing her up.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.130
<i>This country grants the underworld 
far too much autonomy.</i>

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:25.130
<i>The mafia places huge bounties 
on parties they want to punish,</i>

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.220
<i>and there are now companies 
trying to make a profit from that.</i>

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.390
<i>Our government and law enforcement 
are letting this happen.</i>

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.770
<i>This just should not be.</i>

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.370
<i>It's an absolute disgrace.</i>

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.530
Hey...

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.850
The hell are you doin'?!

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.480
Damn it!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.290
Good evening. Fancy meeting you here.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.050
Hey, hey.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.810
Hey there! Great job today.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.500
Hi.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.830
Yes. They're headed there now.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:06:59.920
Chateau.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.940
We're only hearing about 
the details of this job today,

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.970
so make sure you stay in line.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.560
Can I get an answer?

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:12.750
Yes, sir.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.480
<i>Eighteenth floor.</i>

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.670
This is who we'd like you to go after.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.250
His name is Ryang-Ha Song.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.850
He appeared about eight years ago.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:33.300
He was an interpreter for the Santoukai, 
a powerful organization in Asia.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.140
Didn't the Santoukai...

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.180
Yes. They disbanded five years ago.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.740
The reason was an incident in which 
Song assassinated their upper echelon.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.510
In a single night, he killed 
18 members of the top brass,

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.320
including their leader.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.450
It caused quite the uproar back then.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.060
He is extremely dangerous.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:58.410
Just the other day, he infiltrated 
one of our trade deals,

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.250
and four people were killed.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:08.690
There are currently over 20 organizations 
that have bounties out on Song,

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.980
but I assure you, we're offering the most.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.710
Please seriously consider entering 
an exclusive contract with us.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.600
I'd heard rumors about this guy,

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.800
but I didn't think we'd 
get an offer for him.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.050
Rumors?

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.690
People seem very desperate 
to take down this Song guy.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:32.810
They're trying to strike deals with 
organizations such as ours.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.820
Are you going to take the deal?

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.600
Well, this job will be good money,

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:42.450
but it seems pretty dangerous.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.610
By the way, no trying to take 
this deal into your own hands.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:49.790
Can I get an answer?

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:56.720
You don't need to worry. 
I'm on another job right now.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:01.910
Listen, Chateau. We're bounty hunters.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.250
We're doing some shady things, 
if I'm being completely honest.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.040
There's a lot of danger and 
putting our lives on the line,

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.300
especially for a young lady.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.380
You really should look 
into other job opportunities.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:20.170
Whoops. Excuse me for a bit. 
My wife's calling.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.340
Could you ask for the check?

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.930
Man, I was getting tired of waiting.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.260
Anyway, I'll take care of this.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.260
There are things I'd like to talk to you about.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.660
Why don't we go somewhere else?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.150
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.640
Don't just stand there. Have a seat.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.150
The fresh fruit juice from this 
little stand is really good.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.020
Oh, was orange okay? 
I just sorta picked one.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.910
This is who I'm currently after.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:11.170
What are your terms?

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.170
Huh...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.280
You sure don't hesitate 
when it comes to stuff like this,

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.010
but you never answer the 
phone when I call you.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.180
Is this the other thing 
you wanted to talk about?

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.780
How much is this guy worth?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.600
He doesn't seem like a big deal.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.690
Exactly what are you after?

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.450
I don't understand.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.700
Why do you keep pursuing me?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.660
Are you mocking me?

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:48.850
Mocking, eh?

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:56.360
I'm offended. I'm just trying 
to get you to notice me.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.720
And...

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.640
You're not going to find 
another patron like me.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.600
I wish you'd be a little 
more courteous toward me.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.200
Oh, sorry. Did that hurt?

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.070
Well, that just won't do.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.290
How am I supposed to hold back 
when you do that so suddenly?

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:32.790
You don't want to get hurt... do you?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.880
What the?

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:34.840
Hey...

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:38.090
Oh, sorry about that. We're just 
having a little lovers' quarrel.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.050
Jeez...

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:44.050
Oh, right. I didn't tell you 
the terms of this deal yet.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:50.310
On the 24th, Christmas Eve,

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.120
go on a date with me.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:31.310
Is something wrong, sir?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.610
Your time isn't up yet...

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.190
Sir?

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.960
H-Hey, wait!

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.320
Wait, what are you doing?!

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.490
Let's see...

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.650
Oh, there it is.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.350
<i>So, hey.</i>

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:06.320
Do I still have time on the clock?

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:13.850
Merry! Merry, merry, merry!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:17.220
Hey... What's the deal with that huge tree?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.220
Merry, merry, merry! Merry, merry!

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.530
What are you talking about, sir?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:22.730
It's Christmas today.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.050
You didn't buy that with 
company funds, did you?

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:26.990
Hello?!

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.840
But you know...

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.140
Why are you trying to change the subject?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:36.120
I never thought Chateau 
would take a day off.

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:41.870
Spending Christmas alone 
with the president... How sad.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.630
Well, what do you want me to do about it?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:47.490
We could at least go buy a cake!

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:49.640
Merry, merry, merry!

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.640
Oh, for crying out loud...

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.180
After we're done with work.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.640
Christmas cake!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:59.150
I thought I told you 3 PM.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.380
It's already 4 PM.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.900
That's pretty bad. Even I would get mad.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:09.070
Well, now that I've upset you, 
I will take my leave for the day.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.410
Hey, I was just kidding! Come on!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.000
That's really not fair, you know.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.220
You could at least think up 
some excuse for being late.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.430
You were probably late 
on purpose, weren't you?

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.200
Hoping that I would've left.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.670
Hey, was I right on the nose? 
You're so mean.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:29.430
But, well... We still have 
some time before dinner.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:31.930
Why don't we wander around?

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.910
Hey, does stuff like this 
interest you at all?

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.440
I've never seen you wear any.

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.950
Not really. It's unnecessary.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:56.700
Aw, but I'd love to give you 
something like that as a gift.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.510
Pointless.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.500
Your ears were pierced.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.840
Aw.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:13.100
I think I feel a little better now.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.630
Hey, you should reopen them.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.160
Hey, want me to reopen them for you?

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.380
Absolutely not.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.980
Aw, why not?

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:31.760
Talk about a hard decision...

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.990
Hm, do you have any recommendations?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.550
On the 24th, Christmas Eve,

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.080
go on a date with me.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.390
What?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.900
You want to make a deal, don't you?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.470
Are you trying to say those are the terms?

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.720
Guess we've got a date, then.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.160
It's a promise.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.850
Hey, is there any in particular you'd prefer?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.770
Come over here and take a look.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.480
Hey.

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.650
Wait up. You're walking way too fast.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:16.690
I can't count this as a date 
if you don't walk next to me.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:18.550
Should we try again on another day?

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.630
That's better.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:32.510
But there are people everywhere.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:36.010
I guess that's to be expected, 
considering the day.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:37.800
You should really

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.960
avoid bringing so much 
attention to yourself.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:46.400
Are you sure you should be walking 
in the middle of town like this?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:52.660
Hm, well, I guess you bring up a good point.

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:55.160
I was hoping to wait 
until we saw all the lights,

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.530
but should we just go to the hotel now?

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.180
You know, so I don't bring 
so much attention to myself.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:02.250
The room I got has a great night view.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:05.290
I also asked that our dinner 
be brought up to the room.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.800
I'll have them serve this cake for dessert.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:09.670
What's the matter?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.060
I'm leaving.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.170
Hey, come on, now.

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:16.850
Are you sure about this? 
You're going to ruin our date.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:17.680
Hey.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.190
Change your mind?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.320
He seemed to be making quite 
a fortune in a rather petty way.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:56.010
He was actually using his lover 
in a badger game in this day in age.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:58.510
I mean, anyone who fell 
for it is an idiot, too.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:00.580
Well?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.640
If you don't mind him being 
a corpse, he's all yours.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.020
You can think of him as a Christmas present.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.000
I have no idea...

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:14.120
how you intend to use me.

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.600
I have no idea why 
I would be of interest to you.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.120
Come on, now. I think 
you've got the wrong idea.

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:25.730
I was just trying to help you out.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.840
You really want to make this 
into some deal, don't you?

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.070
Nothing is more frightening 
than something that's free.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:33.380
That's quite a quote.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.500
Well, if you insist...

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.880
Let's go back to discussing this deal.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.180
All right, let's have dinner.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.840
Wow, it's pretty late.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.080
Those children were very good at singing.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.830
You mean the hymn that the choir sang.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.910
The LEDs were pretty, too.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.170
Just call them decorative lights.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.630
If only Chateau had joined us...

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.340
Too bad.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.450
She said she'd be at work tomorrow.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.880
<i>Ryang-Ha Song?</i>

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:32.230
<i>Come on... You've gotta 
be kidding me, Chateau.</i>

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.810
What's the matter, sir?

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:38.050
This is far enough.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.650
Huh? But why?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.070
I'll walk you to the platform.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:42.950
I'll even walk you home—

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.390
This is far enough.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.660
How cruel.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:52.330
I canceled staying the night at the hotel 
since you said you had to work tomorrow...

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:57.570
The receptionist looked at 
me with such sympathy.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:01.690
I'm so hurt. How disappointing.

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:03.610
It was so expensive.

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:06.850
Too bad. So sad.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:06.850
<i>Shut up...</i>

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.790
Oh, yeah.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:11.980
One sec. Let me just confirm one thing.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:14.440
Huh?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:19.900
Pardon me.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.910
I knew it.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.060
Your scent doesn't bother me.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:36.490
Everyone else smells putrid to me.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:39.920
I wonder why you're fine, though.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:58.970
<i>If the final stop in this romance 
is made up of your tears,</i>

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:09.860
<i>the path we go down will have 
flowers of death in full bloom.</i>

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:08.570
17 Years Ago

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:19.110
We've found the suspicious vehicle 
from the report. Over.

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:41.690
Little girl, can you tell me your name?

00:23:37.550 --> 00:23:39.700
Next episode: "Target."
